OBSERVATIONS (not FAIL grounds — pre-existing oracle property, not
introduced by this attempt, and backstopped by a deterministic check in
the same oracle run):
- CHECK 7's coverage of successRateTextClass's mid-tier colors (lime/
  yellow/orange) is stochastic: it depends on the Monte Carlo engine's
  randomized simulation landing a success rate in 60-89% on that one page
  load, and silently misses the mutation when the CSS build is stale
  (unsafelisted class -> inherited color -> trivially passes contrast).
  CHECK 9 (emitter_coverage.py) reliably catches the same mutation every
  time regardless, so the oracle as a whole is not compromised, but a
  future task could make CHECK 7 deterministic (fixed MC seed or a
  fixture forcing each tier) rather than relying on CHECK 9 as the sole
  reliable backstop.
- TestSuccessRateClasses (pre-existing, untouched by U6) only asserts the
  tier-name substring ("lime"/"yellow"/"orange"), not the specific shade,
  so it would pass identically whether the -700 darkening were present or
  reverted. Not introduced by this attempt; flagging for the backlog if a
  future task touches this function again.
